# G129 — Watermarking Application

*v2. See `watermark.md` for prose: LSB steganography with length header,
capacity as pure function, position ADT with Tiled as mode, alpha-blend
formula shared with G123.*

---

## Choreographic Case: Vault Image Fingerprint

[fingerprint @original-path @metadata @output-path
    IN ORDER TO
        embed provenance metadata into an image via LSB steganography
        so the artifact carries its own verifiability
        without visibly changing the image

    @original <- [img[load {path: @original-path}]]
    @payload  <- [cbor[encode {data: @metadata}]]

    @capacity <- [wm[lsb-capacity {image: @original, bits-per-channel: 2}]]
    @payload
        where length at most @capacity
        || -> #error "payload too large: " + @payload:length +
                     " bytes, capacity is " + @capacity

    @fingerprinted <- [wm[embed-lsb {image: @original,
                                       payload: @payload,
                                       bits-per-channel: 2}]]
    [img[save {path: @output-path, image: @fingerprinted}]]
]

[verify-fingerprint @path @expected-metadata
    IN ORDER TO
        recover the embedded metadata and check it against the expected

    @img <- [img[load {path: @path}]]
    @recovered <- [wm[extract-lsb {image: @img, bits-per-channel: 2}]]
                  || -> #error "image has no recoverable fingerprint"
    @metadata <- [cbor[decode {data: @recovered}]]

    @metadata
        where equal to @expected-metadata
        -> #verified
        || -> #tampered
]

---

## Choreographic Case: Visible Copyright Overlay

[copyright-overlay @photo @logo @position
    IN ORDER TO
        composite a visible copyright watermark at the requested position

    [wm[apply-visible-watermark {base: @photo,
                                   watermark: @logo,
                                   position: @position,
                                   opacity: 180}]]
]

---

## Verb Surface

[wm
    lsb-capacity               {image, bits-per-channel}
    embed-lsb                  {image, payload, bits-per-channel}   ;; || payload-too-large, invalid-bits
    extract-lsb                {image, bits-per-channel}            ;; || truncated-data
    apply-visible-watermark    {base, watermark, position, opacity}
    resolve-position           {base, watermark, position}
]

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: position is a bare-word string

The v1 modeled `Position::{TopLeft, TopRight, BottomLeft, BottomRight,
Center, Tiled}` as an enum. In Innate, the position is a bare-word
string the resolver interprets, with Tiled carrying the "mode" semantic:

[wm[apply-visible-watermark {base: @photo, watermark: @logo,
                              position: "bottom-right", opacity: 180}
    where
        "top-left" | "top-right" | "bottom-left" | "bottom-right" | "center"
            place the watermark once at that corner
        and "tiled" repeats the watermark across the base
            with raster iteration (row-major) by watermark dimensions
]

---

## Capacity as pure function, checked before embed

[wm[lsb-capacity {image: @img, bits-per-channel: @n}
    where
        capacity-bytes = (pixels × 3 × n) / 8 - 4   (minus length header)
        and n is 1, 2, 3, or 4
            (higher n = more capacity, more visible speckle)
]

Callers check capacity first; the embed itself resists on overflow.

---

## Graceful failure on tampered header

[wm[extract-lsb {image: @suspect-img, bits-per-channel: 2}
    || -> #warn "header decoded to an impossible length; image is not a carrier"
        ;; resolver checks bits.len >= 32 + payload_len × 8 before slicing
        ;; never reads beyond the image's bit capacity
]

---

## Demo

[demo
    @base <- [img[filled {width: 32, height: 32,
                            color: {r: 128, g: 128, b: 128}}]]

    -> [wm[lsb-capacity {image: @base, bits-per-channel: 1}]]    ;; -> 380
    -> [wm[lsb-capacity {image: @base, bits-per-channel: 2}]]    ;; -> 764
    -> [wm[lsb-capacity {image: @base, bits-per-channel: 4}]]    ;; -> 1532

    @payload <- "Hello, watermark!"
    @embedded <- [wm[embed-lsb {image: @base, payload: @payload,
                                  bits-per-channel: 1}]]
    @extracted <- [wm[extract-lsb {image: @embedded, bits-per-channel: 1}]]
    -> @extracted == @payload                                     ;; -> true

    @logo <- [img[filled {width: 8, height: 8, color: {r: 255, g: 0, b: 0}}]]
    @branded <- [wm[apply-visible-watermark
                     {base: @base, watermark: @logo,
                      position: "top-right", opacity: 128}]]
    -> [img[get {image: @branded, x: 31, y: 0}]]
    ;; -> {r: 191, g: 63, b: 63}   (128/128/128 blended with 255/0/0 at α=128)
]
